{
  "source": "Prompts/layers-2.mp4",
  "duration": 170.6666875,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.5,
      "text": "Think back to English class. Have you ever read a confusing passage that you had to read"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.5,
      "end": 10.3,
      "text": "two or three times before it made any sense at all? Take a look at this sentence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.0,
      "end": 17.06,
      "text": "The horse raced past the barn fell. On the first read, it feels broken. So you read it again,"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.58,
      "end": 22.66,
      "text": "testing different interpretations. Did the barn fall? On the third read, the structure"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.66,
      "end": 28.86,
      "text": "resolves. Someone raced a horse past a barn and then fell. Human comprehension relies on"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.86,
      "end": 33.1,
      "text": "updating meaning incrementally, refining the context until the pieces fit."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.98,
      "end": 37.8,
      "text": "Artificial intelligence does something mathematically similar, using a sequence"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.8,
      "end": 43.36,
      "text": "of operations called layers. This neural network passes data through a stack of sequential layers"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.36,
      "end": 49.44,
      "text": "to process text. Inside each layer, attention and transformation calculate how your words relate."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.14,
      "end": 54.96,
      "text": "The AI represents words as a starting row of decimal numbers. Across the columns,"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.96,
      "end": 59.38,
      "text": "notice how these decimal values shift and change significantly layer by layer."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.98,
      "end": 66.56,
      "text": "These shifting decimals are the machine equivalent of rereading a text. The AI is incrementally"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.56,
      "end": 72.82,
      "text": "updating the contextual meaning of the words at each mathematical step. Let's trace an example on"
    },
    {
      "start": 72.82,
      "end": 79.34,
      "text": "this board. The cat sat on the mat because it was tired. Focus on the ambiguous word,"
    },
    {
      "start": 79.34,
      "end": 86.14,
      "text": "it. Its starting numbers don't reveal the pronouns reference. But moving through layers 1 and 2, the"
    },
    {
      "start": 86.14,
      "end": 91.92,
      "text": "numbers update, capturing specific mathematical connections to cat, building over successive"
    },
    {
      "start": 91.92,
      "end": 98.44,
      "text": "layers. Pause the video for a moment. If the AI is trying to link these words, what must happen"
    },
    {
      "start": 98.44,
      "end": 104.08,
      "text": "to those decimals for the sentence to finally make sense? Here is the result. By this final"
    },
    {
      "start": 104.08,
      "end": 109.22,
      "text": "stage, the decimals for the word it have been transformed to align with the mathematical"
    },
    {
      "start": 109.22,
      "end": 114.4,
      "text": "patterns associated with the word cat. Because those numerical values now match,"
    },
    {
      "start": 114.82,
      "end": 119.06,
      "text": "the AI interprets the pronoun as the specific animal from earlier in the sentence."
    },
    {
      "start": 119.7,
      "end": 125.1,
      "text": "Real-world AI models operate at an enormous scale. Companies deploy dozens,"
    },
    {
      "start": 125.5,
      "end": 129.22,
      "text": "sometimes over a hundred sequential layers to process complex language."
    },
    {
      "start": 129.64,
      "end": 135.86,
      "text": "If a simple horse sentence takes three reads, imagine untangling sarcasm, story twists,"
    },
    {
      "start": 136.12,
      "end": 141.42,
      "text": "or complicated logic. AI requires massive layer depth to compute these relationships."
    },
    {
      "start": 142.24,
      "end": 147.24,
      "text": "So why can't developers just add infinite layers to make the AI perfectly understand everything?"
    },
    {
      "start": 147.94,
      "end": 153.22,
      "text": "Because we hit strict physical limitations. Processing data through more layers requires"
    },
    {
      "start": 153.22,
      "end": 159.1,
      "text": "exponentially more computing power and processing time. The extra benefit and comprehension always"
    },
    {
      "start": 159.1,
      "end": 164.58,
      "text": "has to be worth that heavy physical cost, meaning builds up layer by layer, attention"
    },
    {
      "start": 164.58,
      "end": 167.18,
      "text": "and transformation, dozens of times."
    }
  ],
